  {
   "key": "0x3C9",
   "name": "PEL data",
   "aliases": [
    "03C9"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "2672"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "4399-4401"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "4427-4429"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "4433-4434"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "4439-4441"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "4444-4446"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "4449-4452"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "4456-4457"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_dac.cpp",
     "function": "write_p3c9"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_dac.cpp",
     "function": "read_p3c9"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Hex 03C9 is the palette data register.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2672",
       "sha": "9e0f62f263b81e422b7be02ecddb9fb9c9e87561941b92d8a2ddf4ac85d1ebd7"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The DAC has 256 registers of 18 bits, showing up to 256 colours from a possible 256K, and each output is driven by a 6-bit DAC.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "4399-4401",
       "sha": "13bcb0426dab9f6c7e6e14403e403843dba27e77669dead7334e5d4458660c09"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "During normal operation the palette address points to one of the 256 data registers, whose value is converted to the three analog outputs.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "4427-4429",
       "sha": "ae933c302ee62a18de119f2ad6a26a7138c4bb72935e39a90cb1040ab476c5bd"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Each data register is 18 bits wide, 6 bits each for red, green and blue, and is reached through the system interface.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "4433-4434",
       "sha": "90a6bae9091c11579c9de17356c39635425d265d4104cca48eb77b5cbf806df7"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Successive bytes written to 03C9 have their 6 least-significant bits concatenated into the 18-bit palette data, red first, then green, then blue.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "4444-4446",
       "sha": "99427e2c5bde08b6c432bf7ef0f3c1094d956a155941607d460b3b0303906cb4"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A read cycle reads three successive bytes from 03C9 holding the colour value, red first, then green, then blue.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "4449-4452",
       "sha": "0433e8f72f41a447056ba0391c39a81fac400e2ef0afa2545474af7070cceddf"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Reading the data register during a write cycle is undefined and can change the palette.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "4456-4457",
       "sha": "ee22514f002d2e4e8e3b5e98522130371df8d716664e75e0bbe9f3386f0ca2e1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Once the address is loaded, successive accesses to the data register increment the address register.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "4439-4441",
       "sha": "015bb02c48d1021fc2987d8ba6dc0c9cc71a363736a7cb28449a2bb42fba1b43"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "9",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "text": "DOSBox-X keeps the six bits and stores one colour per byte, but with 8-bit DAC emulation enabled it stores all eight bits of a byte instead.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_dac.cpp",
       "lines": "316-317",
       "sha": "808f203990b268e2f508377395555b28e3727884f231ec10fdcf41aa1f74ef9c"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_dac.cpp",
       "lines": "324-333",
       "sha": "7c2a59c96ea8d573f2ac07a47779debcedb673ca36917135089845d7abf9cec5"
      }
     ],
     "row": "4"
    },
    {
     "n": "10",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "After the third byte the read index is set to the write index; outside MCGA double-buffering a completed colour schedules a palette refresh.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_dac.cpp",
